e</description></item><item><title>Asia-US West Coast container spot rates fall below $8,000 as US avoids LA-Long Beach port strike</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/asia-us-west-coast-container-spot-rates-fall-below-8-000-as-us-avoids-5c78e75390/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/asia-us-west-coast-container-spot-rates-fall-below-8-000-as-us-avoids-5c78e75390/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:18:32 +0000</pubDate><category>Rates &amp; Market</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>FMCSA denies hazmat response company’s request for hours-of-service exemption</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/fmcsa-denies-hazmat-response-company-s-request-for-hours-of-service-ex-3efee35725/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/fmcsa-denies-hazmat-response-company-s-request-for-hours-of-service-ex-3efee35725/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:58:26 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>CDLLife</description></item><item><title>DOT watchdog refers 20 motor carrier cases for prosecution in 6 months</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/dot-watchdog-refers-20-motor-carrier-cases-for-prosecution-in-6-months-cfc8664d55/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/dot-watchdog-refers-20-motor-carrier-cases-for-prosecution-in-6-months-cfc8664d55/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:26:57 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>The U.S. Department of Transportation&#x27;s Office of Inspector General referred 20 motor carrier-related cases for criminal or civil prosecution between April 1 and Sept. 30, 2026, according to its semiannual report to Congress. Six of the cases involved falsified or altered inspection records, six involved fraudulent registrations or chameleon carriers, and one each involved attempted bribery, CDL violations, drug and alcohol program violations and driver qualification issues.

